      "message": "If decoding a name string fails, the inner iterator leaves rc set. The outer loop then runs its increment and attempts another decode, which can overwrite the original error (for example, -EOVERFLOW becomes -EINVAL when the field pointer is null). Consider stopping the outer loop when rc is already nonzero, and test a malformed first effecter when the PDR declares multiple effecters.",
